# Canonical site URL — override for preview deploys
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://mannydevelops.com

# ─── Resend (Phase 1A — inquiry form) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# https://resend.com — sign up, verify mannydevelops.com (DKIM/SPF),
# create an API key under https://resend.com/api-keys
RESEND_API_KEY=
INQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL=inquiry@mannydevelops.com
INQUIRY_TO_EMAIL=hello@mannydevelops.com

# ─── Kit / ConvertKit (Phase 1B — email lists) ─────────────────────────────────
# https://app.kit.com — create three forms (Presets, Pricing guide, Newsletter)
# with auto-responder sequences. The "Sticky" capture posts into the Presets
# form by default — set KIT_FORM_STICKY_ID to override.
# Find the API key: Settings → Advanced → V3 API key.
# Find form IDs: open each form → URL ends with /forms/<id>/edit
KIT_API_KEY=
KIT_FORM_PRESETS_ID=
KIT_FORM_PRICING_GUIDE_ID=
KIT_FORM_NEWSLETTER_ID=
KIT_FORM_STICKY_ID=

# ─── Cloudflare Turnstile (Phase 1A — spam protection, optional) ───────────────
# https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/turnstile
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# ─── Cal.com scheduler (Phase 2A — Contact /scheduler) ────────────────────────
# https://cal.com — create 3 event types matching the tabs on /contact:
#   * 15-min Discovery call (free)
#   * 30-min Wedding consult (free)
#   * 45-min Studio visit (Manhattan)
# Each "cal link" is just `{username}/{event-slug}` from the event's URL.
# Defaults are baked into the contact page; set these only to override for a
# preview deploy or staging.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CAL_LINK_DISCOVERY=manuel-pena-i7ohok/15min
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CAL_LINK_WEDDING=manuel-pena-i7ohok/30min
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CAL_LINK_STUDIO=manuel-pena-i7ohok/45min

# ─── Stripe (Phase 2B — shop checkout) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Shop CTAs use Stripe Payment Links, which are just URLs — no API keys needed
# for the client-side flow. Each print SKU (size × edition) and the paid preset
# pack get their own Payment Link, created in the Stripe dashboard:
# https://dashboard.stripe.com/payment-links
#
# Once each link is live, paste its URL into `lib/content.ts`:
#   PRINTS[i].checkoutLinks = { "16×20": "https://buy.stripe.com/...", ... }
#   PRESET_PACKS[i].checkoutLink = "https://buy.stripe.com/..."
#
# Prints without a checkoutLink show "Inquire ↗" linking to /contact, so a
# partial rollout is safe — fill in URLs at your own pace.
#
# These keys are only needed if you later add a Stripe webhook for digital
# fulfillment (Phase 2B.2 — not wired yet):
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
